- The grain is only modestly sampled: 2.7 to 2.9 px is above the 2 px limit but below the 3 px ideal. The contrast may therefore be slightly biased low.
- The script printed RuntimeWarnings (divide by zero and invalid value) in the autocorrelation normalization, at lags with zero overlap count. The fitted lags appear unaffected, but I did not verify this.
- The envelope flattening and the PTC-based K are my own choices, so treat CONTRAST_CORR as approximate.

